From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dcasati <dcasati@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:43:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] ath12k: skip 6 GHz reg rebuild on authorize in strict
 regulatory mode

On ASSOC->AUTHORIZED the driver rebuilds the stored regulatory rules to
pick a 6 GHz client power type.  Under lkpi_regulatory_strict any rule
rebuild revokes TX terminally, so every successful connection lost TX.
Strict station rules exclude 6 GHz; skip the rebuild as add_interface
already does.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 sys/contrib/dev/athk/ath12k/mac.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/contrib/dev/athk/ath12k/mac.c b/sys/contrib/dev/athk/ath12k/mac.c
index a1164052..1aa8cbf5 100644
--- a/sys/contrib/dev/athk/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/sys/contrib/dev/athk/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -7324,6 +7324,14 @@ static int ath12k_mac_handle_link_sta_state(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 		}
 
 		if (ath12k_wmi_supports_6ghz_cc_ext(ar) &&
+#ifdef __FreeBSD__
+		    /*
+		     * This rebuilds the stored rules only to pick 6 GHz client
+		     * power types; strict station rules exclude 6 GHz, and a
+		     * rebuild here would terminally revoke TX.
+		     */
+		    !hw->wiphy->lkpi_regulatory_strict &&
+#endif
 		    arvif->ahvif->vdev_type == WMI_VDEV_TYPE_STA) {
 			link_conf = ath12k_mac_get_link_bss_conf(arvif);
 			reg_info = ab->reg_info[ar->pdev_idx];
-- 
